[35.4163, "o", "64:### `orders`\r\n65-`order_id, customer_id, ordered_at, kind, amount_cents, _load_job, _loaded_at`. `kind` is `box` (the weekly box,\r\n66-charged by billing at 05:30 on the customer's billing weekday; `ordered_at` is the charge) or `addon` (an extra item,\r\n67-ordered at any time). Each order exists in the order system, which the loaders read, from its `ordered_at` on.\r\n68-The nightly `legacy_orders` job writes the table: each run selects orders from the order system and sends them to\r\n69-`orders` in one transaction.\r\n70-\r\n71-### `tickets`\r\n"]
[35.416397, "o", "72-`ticket_id, customer_id, opened_at, topic, _loaded_at`: support tickets, written by change data capture from the\r\n73-support desk 1 to 30 seconds after `opened_at`.\r\n74-\r\n75-### `status_snapshots`\r\n76-`customer_id, snapshot_date, status, _loaded_at`: the billing system's account status (`active`, `paused`,\r\n77-`payment_failed` or `cancelled`) at the end of day `snapshot_date`. Billing records a row for a customer on the\r\n78-sign-up day, on every day the status changed, and on the first day of every month, up to the cancellation (a\r\n79-`cancelled` row is the customer's last); there is at most one row per customer and date.\r\n80-`billing_export` writes each day's partition (all the rows dated D) in one transaction.\r\n81-\r\n82-### `labels`\r\n83-`customer_id, as_of, churned_30d, _loaded_at`: the outcome of a prediction (`customer_id` and `as_of` as in\r\n84-`scoring_points`): `churned_30d` is 1 if the customer cancelled in `(as_of, as_of + 30 days]`, else 0. The outcome\r\n85-becomes known at the cancellation, or when"]
[35.41646, "o", " the 30 days have passed without one.\r\n86-`label_job` writes, in one transaction per run, a row for each prediction whose outcome became known before the run\r\n87-started and that has no row yet.\r\n"]
